    "complaint_id": "9681442-2025-00066",
    "complaint_text": "On the first case of using the phaco machine, a smell of burning was noticed. The battery after being on charge all night had to be changed as it was showing as low battery. Water was not entering the cassette from the BSS resulting in air coming out and releasing bubbles. All equipment was checked for any kinks or signs of blockage, this was all normal. The handpiece was changed to a new one and the tubing changed to a new one unopened box. The current case was ended to restart to allow for a prime and tune. The prime and tune was successful. The water did go into the cassette, however it was continuing to release air bubbles. These issues were noted on three cases and a decision made to stop surgery. \u00c3\u0192\u00c2\u00a2\u00c3\u00a2\u00e2\u20ac\u0161\u00c2\u00ac\u00c3\u00a2\u00e2\u201a\u00ac\u00c5\u201c No Error Codes given. (SYS05783)  Additional information requested.    Additional Information:  Patient involvement: No  Patient Injury:  No",
